#82200
"Mountain Ledge - Before a Carved Cliff Face"
"The mountain ledge, while remaining fairly flat and level, narrows here before
yet another cliff face carved with handholds.  The predatory activity evident
further south is in evidence here as well; the inch-deep covering of snow has
been packed down in places with tracks of an enormous cat.  Far in the
distance to the east, the frozen wall stretches onward below, a monolith of
solid ice stretching for miles.

An ancient, stone marker which has been deliberately defaced lies near the
cliff face to the north.
"
""
