#82201
"Cliff Ledge - Dragonspire Panorama"
"From this highest point along the mountain trail, the marvelous panorama of
the Dragonspires yawns all around.  This ledge is wide, probably twenty paces,
and quite level.  A brisk but not harsh wind prevents any fine dusting of
powder from collecting here, although a thin covering of ice-glazed snow has
managed to adhere itself to the rock.  Below to the east, the frozen wall
stretches for miles, the fangs of the Eastern Dragonspires stretching beyond. 
For what seems like eternity to the south, the cloud-shrouded peaks of the
Dragonspires can be seen, stretching from the east to the west side of the
horizon.  The cliff ledge continues to the north, where the deeper snow has
seen more traffic.  Immediately to the south, the ledge ends abruptly in a
sheer cliff face, but someone or something long ago carved convenient
handholds, allowing an easy climb to another ledge below.
"
""
