E
"knee-deep snow tread tracks troll ogre"
"The tracks lead both north and south from here in what would be knee-deep
snow.  As packed down as the snow is, and as many prints are evident, it would
appear that this area experiences extremely heavy traffic leading south along
the ledge and north into the cavern tunnel from here.  The tracks are almost
certainly ogrish or trollish in size and weight.
"
E
"carved tunnel 1 north"
"The tunnel has been crudely carved directly into the stone face of the
mountain.  Marks on the floor and uneven chisel work make it quite obvious
where segments of heavy basalt had to be chipped away and where the floor and
walls are naturally level.  The ground in the center of the tunnel has been
worn smooth with the tread of ages.
"
