#82203
"Carved Cavern Tunnel"
"Crudely chipped basalt has been worn smooth by the tread of passing feet under
this carved archway through the volcano wall.  Evidence of the carving work is
easier to make out along the walls and ceiling, where traffic has not worn the
stone smooth.  Against the eastern wall, tiny bone fragments have accumulated;
a long-dried, crimson smear against the wall and the occasional shattered
fragment of a weapon reveal that this tunnel has seen frequent combat.  A
narrower tunnel west of here appears to serve as a guardpost.  As one ventures
south back into the weather, the snow and ice resumes, while to the north, a
cinder-strewn trail meanders around the crater floor.
"
"[Nereus] Checks for cflag 152, 153 here - if either is true, sound alarm!
[Nereus] Elves, dwarves, halflings - sound alarm!
[Nereus] ** Room Finished **
if reputations are ever fixed, won't cflag 153 (and maybe 152) be redundant? 
-Talis
