#82205
"Trail Along the Volcano Floor"
"This fork along the volcano floor appears to see much activity.  Large,
humanoid footprints can be seen trampling the cinder-strewn, rock floor.  In
true trollish fashion, debris considered unedible for one reason or another
has been thrown carelessly along the ground, mostly winding up piled against
the smooth, basalt wall to the north.  A cinder-strewn trail continues east
and west, wet from melting snow, presumably from persons travelling from the
south into the center of the volcano proper.  To the south, a smooth stone
tunnel leads out of the volcano, into the whipping winter winds.
"
""
