#82206
"Trail Along the Volcano Floor - Guardpost"
"Once probably a mere crack for escaping magma from deeper in the mountain,
this section of the trail along the volcano floor has been widened roughly
enough to fit a horse comfortably through this area.  The eastern wall has
been worn away, both from what appears to have been a half-hearted attempt at
chiseling away a bench and the everyday wear of someone or something leaning
lazily against the wall.  Unlike the wider, cinder-strewn trail to the north
and west from here, the dark rock above forms a ceiling here, crudely carved
out by rough tools.  To the west, the trail becomes more wet, most likely due
to those tracking snow into the volcano floor from the snowy outdoors.
"
""
