#82207
"Trail Along the Volcano Floor - Fork in the Trail"
"Forking south from its east-west course through the bustling interior of the
settlement, the trail also leads south through a makeshift guardpost and out
of the village further to the south.  Like elsewhere in the settlement, debris
has accumulated against the bases of the walls, items discarded when their
owner was bored with them.  High above, the grey, wintry skies can be seen,
but here between the sheltering basalt walls of the volcano, there is little
wind or weather from above.  Further west, a bustling gathering place is
evident, where the gutteral sounds of conversation and the noises of mundane
life can be heard.  To the east, a great deal of clutter has collected along
the southern wall and an alcove, where a makeshift storeroom has sprung into
being.
"
"[Nereus] ** Room Finished **
"
