#82208
"Trail Along the Volcano Floor - Cluttered Alcove"
"An overhang along the eastern wall roughly twenty feet up offers shelter from
weather above, but it seems unlikely the inhabitants of this settlement took
the weather into consideration when designating this section of the trail as a
storeroom of sorts.  Both sides of the trail have been arbitrarily piled with
various articles, although a rough organization appears to divide the articles
along the southern wall into crude tools, and the eastern wall, beneath the
alcove, pelts and roughly carved blocks of stone.  The ground here is strewn
with cinders, assorted debris, and there are a few droppings from what appear
to be large rats.  The trail continues north and west, winding along the
volcano floor.
"
"[Nereus] Room 82226 is east of here but only accessible through acodes
