#82210
"Trail Along the Volcano Floor - Beneath an Overhang"
"The cinder-strewn trail winds its way from south to west here, beneath an
overhanging eastern wall.  The dark basalt walls continue for perhaps a
hundred feet above the volcano floor before the wintry, grey sky can finally
be made out high above.  A narrow cavern entrance has been carved to the
north, leading into what seems from here to be a small, cozy cavern, the dim
glow of embers visible from inside.  The overhang continues along the trail to
the south, while the trail to the west appears to have been completely swept
clean of the cinders found here.
"
"[Nereus] ** Last room, finished on 26 March 2003 **
"
