#82211
"Comfortably Warm Cavern"
"This warm, homey cavern is not what one might expect in a settlement of
trolls.  A hearth, carefully shielded by several crude blocks of basalt, glows
softly warm in a corner of this rounded cave.  A few well-made rugs and thick
white pelts cover the stone cavern floor, clean and well kept.  The cavern is
small, probably fifteen paces to a side, round, and has a ceiling roughly
eight feet high, but whoever lives here is clearly given great respect to have
their own personal living space.  To the south, the cinder-covered floor of
the crater winds past.
"
""
