#82212
"Trail Picked Clean Along the Volcano Floor"
"A shiny, worn section of the dark, basalt ground here and a depression in the
center are the only signs that mark the trail as it winds along the floor of
the volcano here.  The flecks of cinders and chips of stone evident elsewhere
along the trail have been picked completely clean, almost as if someone has
regularly swept the area for debris.  On both sides of the floor, the smooth,
dark basalt walls of the volcano rise to the sky, leaving a window of grey sky
high above.  To the east, cinders have been strewn along the trail again as it
winds southward.
"
"[Nereus] children don't go past here unless under attack
[Nereus] ** Room Finished **
