#82213
"Clean-swept Trail Along the Volcano Floor - Rock Pile"
"The smooth basalt floor here has been picked clean of the cinders found
elsewhere around the volcano floor, and the cause is evident here: someone or
something has stacked a huge collection of rocks against the base of the
eastern wall.  The larger rocks have generally been piled along the bottom of
the stack, although there is no apparent reason to how they have been
stacked.  A trail, evident only by a track worn even smoother along the basalt
floor, leads south to west from here, or to the north, a wide cavern entrance
has been roughly carved leading into what appears to be a communal cavern of
sorts.
"
"[Nereus] ** Room Finished **
[Nereus] Sometimes the children sleep here too
"
