#82214
"Communal Sleeping Cavern"
"A yawning cavern entrance, ten feet high and twice as wide, opens to the south
of what obviously serves as a communal sleeping cavern.  The cavern widens
slightly as it opens just north of the southern entrance and peaks at roughly
ten feet in height before narrowing to a mere crack at its northern end. 
There are no chisel marks evident along the walls, ceiling, or floor, although
the floor has been worn smooth both by the tramp of trollish foot and sleeping
trolls laying along the ground here.  The cavern appears to be naturally
formed, the rock made of the same dark gray basalt visible elsewhere in the
interior of this volcano.
"
"[Nereus] ** Room Finished **
"
