#82215
"Trail Along the Volcano Floor"
"Marked merely by a segment of the crater floor which has been worn smoother
than that around it, the trail here stretches east to west, swept almost
completely free of cinders and other debris.  The dark basalt walls of the
volcano stretch high above to the north and south, the outer wall of some
ancient crater north of you, and a newer, darker basalt wall of the most
geologically recent crater to the south.  To the east, the debris-free trail
continues, while to the west, some clutter is evident.  High above, the sky is
visible, a faint dusting of snow drifting past.  Perhaps being a bit
underground keeps the temperature here warm enough to keep the snow from
accumulating.
"
"[Nereus] children don't go past here
[Nereus] ** Room Finished **
"
