#82216
"Trail Along the Volcano Floor"
"The trail winds around a sharp corner, created by lava flows ages ago and worn
smooth by the tread of countless feet.  A side tunnel leads west from here,
but a hanging curtain of pelts stitched together blocks a good view of what
might lie beyond.  The debris along the walls here seems less evident than in
other places along the trail, although why this section is less littered than
others is a mystery.  A terrible stench, bloody footprints, and visible heaps
of what look like carcasses are evident along the cinder-strewn trail further
south.  To the east, the trail continues as well, although it looks to have
been swept free of the cinders that are spread about the trail here.
"
"[Nereus] ** Room Finished **
"
