#82217
"Cramped, Messy Cavern - Traveller's Home"
"Marginally cleaner than the remainder of the trollish settlement, this
cramped, messy cavern has been carved directly from the basalt walls that
define the sides of the volcano.  Probably once little more than an alcove in
the rock, it has been roughly chiseled until it has formed a room roughly ten
feet long and a bit less across.  Debris has been piled along the southern
side of the room: collections of pieces of rock, teeth from various animals,
furs, the strings of instruments, woodcarving implements, and other wooden
pegs and pieces.  Along the northern wall, a rumpled pile of furs has been
laid along the ground and presumably serves as a bed.  A curtain made from
various pelts stitched together prevents some of the sounds and smells of the
troll settlement from entering the cavern.
"
"[Nereus] bard trainer potentially, if someone needs one
[Nereus] ** Room Finished **
"
