#82220
"Trail Along the Volcano Floor"
"This section of the crater floor seems to serve as an extended storeroom for
what appears to be a stable to the west.  Apparently not concerned with
organization or weather, the trolls seem to have left all manner of what they
would consider tools piled in various heaps along the edges of the trails. 
Ruts from carts are evident against the southern crater wall, likely a place
where a cart or carts have been left.  The cinder-strewn rock of the volcano
floor continues east and north from here, while a cave mouth opens to the west.
"
