#82221
"Trail Along the Volcano Floor - Fork in the Trail"
"The cinder-strewn trail along the volcano floor forks here, heading east-west
through the bustling interior of the settlement, or through a narrow
checkpoint leading out of the village to the south.  Similar to elsewhere
along the volcano trail, debris has been strewn haphazardly along the base of
the northern wall, where someone has scrawled what might be a face, perhaps
etched into the stone by a child.  The din of chatter and mundane activity can
be heard from the east, where what appears to be a central gathering place can
be seen, while even more clutter lines the volcano walls further west.
"
""
