#82222
"Trail Along the Volcano Floor - Guardpost"
"This narrowing of the path along the volcano floor appears to serve as a
checkpoint for people who are entering the bustling center of this small
settlement.  A long, smooth outcropping of rock, half-carved, half-worn away
by trolls, has been formed into a bench along the western wall here, giving a
place for the disgruntled trolls assigned guard duty to rest.  Much like the
trail east and north of here, sanitation of the community does not seem to be
enforced or even contemplated; debris is strewn about along the eastern wall
and piled under the stone bench.  The dry cinder-strewn volcano floor
continues to the north, while to the east it is more wet, probably from those
tracking melting snow in from the south.
"
"[Nereus] ** Room Finished **
acode 2, adata 2 needs to be empty-handed, not empty handed -Talis
