#82223
"Cavern Through the Volcano Wall"
"Despite being a far cry from a well-maintained stable in a human settlement,
this carved cavern obviously serves as a supply room of sorts for the raising
of animals.  Piles of crude stone tools that might almost be referred to as
farming implements are visible strewn carelessly against walls or just dropped
on the ground when not in use.  This cavern probably was once a narrow crack
leading from the interior of the volcano to the outside, but the basalt walls
have been carved smooth by crude tools of some sort.  The low basalt ceiling
has been worn smooth; only seven or so feet tall, it requires the trolls of
the region to duck or, as the smoothness indicates, hit their head.  The
crumbly rock of the interior is visible eastward towards the center of the
volcano, while a snow-covered ledge can be seen past a stone gate to the west.
"
"[Nereus] Acode #1 is for someone attacking the animals west
"
