#82226
"Small Cavern - Animal Den"
"This small, dark, dank chamber obviously serves as the den for at least a few
and possibly dozens of fairly small animals.  The rocky ground is covered in
bits of shredded cloth and masses of fine, tiny white hairs.  Beneath the
nest-like hair and cloth substance, the ground is covered in a damp sort of
mulch, probably the decay of organic material brought into this den.  The
southern side of the cavern seems to have less nesting material, but is
covered in pellet-shaped droppings.  A narrow squeeze leads out of this cavern
to the west, the unknown lying beyond.
"
"[Nereus] ** Room Finished **
